title: Heidelberg Votes
subtitle: The congress decides on the theses.
new-page: true
tags: event
view-if: congress_heidelberg = 2
max-visits: 1
priority: 9
on-arrival: {!
RG.congressEnd();
var total = Math.max(1, Q.congress_delegates_total);
Q.heid_support = Q.congress_votes_for;
Q.heid_for = Math.round(total * Q.congress_votes_for / 100);
Q.heid_against = Math.max(0, Math.round(total * (100 - Q.congress_votes_for) / 100));
Q.heid_ul_won = (Q.congress_result == 'ultraleft') ? 1 : 0;
Q.heid_pass = 0;
if (Q.heid_ul_won) {
    Q.heidelberg_outcome = 3;
} else if (Q.heid_motion == 1) {
    Q.heid_pass = 1;
} else {
    Q.heidelberg_outcome = 2;
    if (Q.congress_result == 'luxemburgist') { Q.election_boycott = 0; }
}
!}

= Heidelberg Votes

On the last evening the delegates vote by raising their mandate cards, district by district, while two tellers from each side count.

[? if heid_ul_won = 0 : The theses are carried by [+ heid_for +] votes to [+ heid_against +]. ?][? if heid_ul_won = 1 : The Left Radicals' motion is carried. The Zentrale had [+ heid_for +] votes, and it was not enough. ?] [? if congress_close_call = 1 : It came down to a handful of mandates, and both sides will say the other cheated. ?]

[? if heid_pass = 1 : Laufenberg rises and declares that the minority will not accept the decision. The Left Radical delegates stand up together and walk towards the door. ?][? if heid_motion = 2 and heid_ul_won = 0 : There is no walkout. The Left Radicals have lost the argument and kept their seats. ?][? if heid_ul_won = 1 : The Spartacist members of the Zentrale have just been voted out of their own party's leadership. ?]

- @walkout: The Left Radicals are leaving.
- @to_result: Continue...

@to_result
view-if: heid_pass = 0
go-to: result

@walkout
title: The Walkout
new-page: true
view-if: heid_pass = 1

= The Walkout

The doors bang behind the Left Radicals. In Hamburg, Bremen and Berlin their districts are waiting for them.

- @let_go: Let them go. The expulsions stand.
- @probation: Call them back: a last chance to submit by the next congress.

@let_go
subtitle: A smaller party, and of one mind. Radek will call it cutting off the left hand.
on-arrival: {!
Q.heidelberg_outcome = 1;
Q.election_boycott = 0;
Q.lean_luxemburgist += 1;
RG.ecci('radek', -6);
!}
go-to: result

@probation
subtitle: [? if heid_radek >= 1 : With Radek's letter behind it, they may take the offer. ?][? if heid_radek = 0 and heid_mandates != 1 : The Left Radicals know the congress was fairly elected. They may listen. ?][? if heid_radek = 0 and heid_mandates = 1 : After a packed congress, they will not believe the offer. ?]
on-arrival: {!
Q.lean_unionist += 2;
Q.election_boycott = 0;
Q.heidelberg_outcome = (Q.heid_radek >= 1 || Q.heid_mandates != 1) ? 2 : 1;
RG.ecci('radek', 6);
RG.ecci('lenin', 4);
!}
go-to: result

@result
title: After Heidelberg
new-page: true
on-arrival: {!
if (Q.heidelberg_outcome == 1) {
    Q.luxemburgist_satisfaction += 10;
    Q.unionist_satisfaction += 4;
    // kept above the generic split threshold: the split itself comes in November
    Q.ultraleft_satisfaction = 12;
    Q.unity -= 5;
    Q.levi_chair = (Q.luxemburg_alive || Q.jogiches_alive) ? 0 : 1;
    RG.news('Heidelberg congress expels the opposition', 3);
    RG.ledger('Heidelberg expelled the Left Radicals.', 'e19_heid_1');
} else if (Q.heidelberg_outcome == 2) {
    if (Q.leading_faction == 'luxemburgist') { Q.junior_faction = 'ultraleft'; }
    Q.ultraleft_satisfaction += 10;
    Q.luxemburgist_satisfaction -= 5;
    Q.unity += 5;
    Q.levi_chair = (Q.luxemburg_alive || Q.jogiches_alive) ? 0 : 1;
    RG.news('Heidelberg ends without a split', 3);
    RG.ledger('Heidelberg kept the Left Radicals in the party.', 'e19_heid_2');
    RG.ecci('radek', 4);
} else {
    Q.leading_faction = 'ultraleft';
    Q.junior_faction = 0;
    Q.levi_chair = 0;
    Q.election_boycott = 1;
    Q.party_chair = (Q.natbol_line == 2) ? 'Heinrich Laufenberg' : 'Otto Rühle';
    RG.setRole(Q.natbol_line == 2 ? 'laufenberg' : 'ruhle', 'Chair of the Zentrale');
    Q.ultraleft_satisfaction += 20;
    Q.luxemburgist_satisfaction = Math.min(Q.luxemburgist_satisfaction, 25);
    Q.unionist_satisfaction -= 10;
    Q.unity -= 8;
    for (var d of Q.districts) {
        Q['district_' + d + '_loyalty'] += (Q['district_' + d + '_faction'] == 'ultraleft') ? 15 : -15;
    }
    RG.news('Left Radicals take the Zentrale at Heidelberg', 3);
    RG.ledger('The Left Radicals won Heidelberg and took the Zentrale.', 'e19_heid_3');
    RG.ecci('lenin', -12);
    RG.ecci('radek', -10);
}
if (Q.levi_chair == 1) { RG.setRole('levi', 'Chair of the Zentrale'); }
Q.kapd_split = 0;
!}

= After Heidelberg

[? if heidelberg_outcome = 1 and heid_already = 1 : The congress adopts the theses without a dissenting vote. The Left Radicals who left in the summer stand outside the party for good. ?][? if heidelberg_outcome = 1 and heid_already = 0 : The congress expels the opposition. The Zentrale will send its own people to rebuild the Left Radical districts. Within weeks it will learn how many members it has lost. ?]

[? if heidelberg_outcome = 2 and election_boycott = 0 : The theses on elections and the unions are adopted, and nobody is expelled for rejecting them. The Left Radicals keep seats in the leadership and their own papers. ?][? if heidelberg_outcome = 2 and election_boycott = 1 : The boycott stands, the theses are shelved, and nobody is expelled. ?]

[? if heidelberg_outcome = 3 : The Spartacists resign from the Zentrale, and a new one is elected from the Left Radical districts with **[+ party_chair +]** at its head. The boycott of parliament and the unions is now the party's line. ?][? if heidelberg_outcome = 3 and luxemburg_alive = 1 : Rosa Luxemburg and Paul Levi stay in the party, at the head of a bitter minority. ?][? if heidelberg_outcome = 3 and luxemburg_alive = 0 : Paul Levi and his friends stay in the party as a bitter minority. ?]
